    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; builds on #514 (already merged).\n\n## What was slow\n\n- Each colour press called `app:getMenuItems()`, which reads the whole DEVONthink menu bar through the macOS accessibility API (every menu, submenu and item, one round trip each). That is the slow part.\n- Then it searched the Format menu for the colour, and `selectMenuItem` walked the path again.\n- There are no fixed delays (`usleep` or `doAfter`) in the colour path, so the menu-bar read dominates.\n- **Not measured.** I cannot run DEVONthink or Hammerspoon from here, so this is from reading the code, not a timing. Use the new benchmark below to see the numbers on your Mac.\n\n## What changes\n\n- One menu-bar read now finds all seven colour items, and their paths are cached.\n- A key press selects the cached path directly, with no menu-bar read.\n- The cache is filled about a second after DEVONthink comes to the front, so even the first press is fast.\n- If the cached item is not found (for example, a colour renamed), the cache is dropped and the menu is read once again. Behaviour and alerts are the same as before.\n- `Cmd+Z` and `Cmd+Shift+Z` are unchanged: their menu titles change with the action, so they cannot be cached. They still read the menu bar on each press.\n- New `DEVONthink.benchmark()` in the Hammerspoon console prints how long the menu-bar read takes and how long a cached selection takes.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [ ] With DEVONthink open, run `DEVONthink.benchmark()` in the Hammerspoon console: note both times (the read is what each press used to cost).\n- [ ] Caps+Option+1 to 7: each picks the right colour, and presses feel faster than before.\n- [ ] The first press right after switching to DEVONthink is also fast.\n- [ ] Rename a colour in DEVONthink's Format menu: the next press still works (one slower press, then fast again).\n- [ ] Caps+c still cycles; Caps+Option+Shift+number still sets the colour only.\n- [ ] Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z still work for highlights.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
